# .npmrc — pnpm fetch config
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIX: ERR_PNPM_FETCH_429 on GitHub codeload tarball (nim-skill)
#
# Root cause: pnpm resolves `github:phamdat721101/nim-skill` to a GitHub
# codeload tarball URL. In CI, unauthenticated burst fetches hit GitHub's
# 429 rate limit. Three defenses applied here:
#
#  1. network-concurrency=1    — serial fetches; eliminates burst that triggers 429
#  2. fetch-retries=5          — override pnpm default (2); survive transient 429s
#  3. fetch-retry-mintimeout   — start backoff at 20s instead of pnpm's 10s default
#  4. fetch-retry-maxtimeout   — cap each retry at 120s (2 min) to avoid hangs
#  5. //codeload.github.com/:_authToken — if GITHUB_TOKEN is set in CI env,
#     pnpm will pick it up and authenticate fetches, lifting the anon rate limit
#     significantly (5000 req/hr authed vs 60 req/hr anon).
#
# Long-term recommendation: publish nim-skill to npm or pin via local `file:`
# path to eliminate the GitHub codeload dependency entirely.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

network-concurrency=1
fetch-retries=5
fetch-retry-mintimeout=20000
fetch-retry-maxtimeout=120000

# GitHub codeload auth — reads GITHUB_TOKEN from env at install time.
# Set GITHUB_TOKEN in your CI/CD secrets (Vercel, Railway, Render, GitHub Actions).
# No-op if the variable is not set (falls back to anonymous fetch with retries above).
//codeload.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
